{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-50371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-50371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}-{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,{t}^{4}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-347617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨7-3t,\\,2{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(1)|?$\n\n$|{r}^{′}(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-347617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=7-3t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-3,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=-3.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=2{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=4t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=4(1)=4.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(-3)}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-347617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-347617" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-347617" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-349469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{2t}(t+1),\\,\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(0)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(0)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-349469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{2t}(t+1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =(2{e}^{2t})(t+1)+{e}^{2t}(1) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}(t+1)+{e}^{2t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(0)=2{e}^{2\\cdot 0}(0+1)+{e}^{2\\cdot 0}=3.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=-\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{9-{0}^{2}}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{x}^{′}(0),\\,{y}^{′}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-349469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-349469" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-349469" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-349469" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-349469" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨{sin}^{3}⁡t,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={sin}^{3}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={cos}^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-50409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refe