ces" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-32417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-9{t}^{2}}}\\,i-20{t}^{3}\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{4}}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t{tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{3}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-50467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩"] ["math" "⟨2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)⟩"] ["math" "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩"] ["math" "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{3}⁡t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-50467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡t)⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-32280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{″}(\\pi )$ if $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-32280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -6({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}^{″}(\\pi )$ by substituting $t=\\pi $ into the above:\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi  \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi \\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-(-1)-0 \\\\ -6\\cdot 1 \\\\ -4\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-32280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-32280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-32280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-32280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-75034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-75034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{3}{t+1} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{3}{(t+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{(t+1)^{2}},\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-75034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-75034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-75034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}},\\,\\frac{-3}{(t+1)^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{-1}{t+1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{-3}{(t+1)^{2}},\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{-3}{t+1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{(t+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-75034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{-3}{(t+1)^{2}},\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-123167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-123167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)={t}^{2}-t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =2t-1 \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-123167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-123167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-123167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2t⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2t-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2t⟩"] ["math" "⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-123167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-69907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the second derivative of $f(t)={e}^{3t+2}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-2{t}^{5}\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-69907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t+2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{5})\\,k \\\\  & =3{e}^{3t+2}\\,i+(-2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,j+(-2\\cdot 5{t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =3{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j-10{t}^{4}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{e}^{3t+2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-10{t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =3(3{e}^{3t+2})\\,i-2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,j-10(4{t}^{3})\\,k \\\\  & =9{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-40{t}^{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-69907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548"} {"question" "q-69907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-69907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{e}^{3t+2}\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-40{t}^{3}\\,k"] ["math" "3{e}^{3t+2}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-10{t}^{3}\\,k"] ["math" "9{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-40{t}^{3}\\,k"] ["math" "9{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j+20{t}^{3}\\,k"] ["math" "{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j+20{t}^{3}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "q-69907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9{e}^{3t+2}\\,i-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j-40{t}^{3}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aabbe12df4d3c2905fca263a94a19a151a234d0e9b0d9ba51535c42f58475a1"} {"question" "e-609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-609.json" "file_sha256" "98c14270d651673c6323e15f9fd74a3d7f3a6ea82687614a1f267ae09c6b4976"} {"question" "e-609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-609.json" "file_sha256" "98c14270d651673c6323e15f9fd74a3d7f3a6ea82687614a1f267ae09c6b4976"} {"question" "e-2398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-2398.json" "file_sha256" "7ec96bbfa821ed234cba2197a000c1dc36384d64a7e6874afd69609553b58d5d"} {"question" "e-2398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-2398.json" "file_sha256" "7ec96bbfa821ed234cba2197a000c1dc36384d64a7e6874afd69609553b58d5d"} {"question" "e-611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-611.json" "file_sha256" "bafb75a05557c0b197170bf084226d09dd0c49e6611067b60d07ffcb6775fefa"} {"question" "e-611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-611.json" "file_sha256" "bafb75a05557c0b197170bf084226d09dd0c49e6611067b60d07ffcb6775fefa"}] "usage" {"e-611" [] "e-2398" [] "e-609" []} "basis" 1260 "retractions" [[17592186198157 :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle$, what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)$?"] [17592186198157 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4$, we have\n$x'(t) = 40t^3$,\nand therefore\n$x'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5$.\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t$, we have\n$y^{′}(t) = \\frac{6}{t}$,\nand therefore\n$y'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12$.\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) &= ⟨x^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}), y^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨5, 12⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186198154 :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t,\\cos t, t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4$."] [17592186198154 :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(t) &= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(\\sin t), \\frac{d}{dt}(\\cos t), \\frac{d}{dt}(t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\cos t,-\\sin t, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right)\n$$\n\nwe substitute\n\n$$\nt=\\dfrac{\\pi}4\n$$\n\ninto the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(\\frac{π}{4}) &= ⟨\\cos (\\frac{π}{4}),-\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}), 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186198158 :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle$, Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t)$."] [17592186198158 :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6$, we have\n$x^{′}(t)|= 6t^{5}; x^{″}(t)|= 30t^{4}$.\n- For $y(t) = t^5$, we have\n$y^{′}(t)|= 5t^{4}; y^{″}(t)|= 20t^{3}$.\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{″}(t) &= ⟨x^{″}(t), y^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨30t^{4}, 20t^{3}⟩ \\\\\n&= 10⟨3t^{4}, 2t^{3}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
